          answer: 'The bottleneck effect; the founder effect. In both, the population that continues is a small, unrepresentative sample of the original gene pool, so genetic variation is reduced.',
          explanation: 'Genetic drift is the mechanism of evolutionary change that is not natural selection; naming its two standard cases keeps a learner from explaining every change in allele frequency as selection.',
