          answer: 'Sedimentary rock. Favourable conditions: rapid burial in sediment such as mud or silt; absence of oxygen so that decomposers cannot act; the presence of hard parts such as bones, teeth or shells. (Any two.)',
          explanation: 'These conditions are also the reason the fossil record has gaps, which is the point a learner must be able to make when a question asks why the record is incomplete.',
