          explanation: 'Slurred speech under the influence of alcohol is therefore a coordination problem (impaired ability of the brain to precisely control the many small muscles involved in speech) rather than a problem with the muscles themselves, which is why the effect reverses once the alcohol is metabolised and cleared from the body.',
