          explanation: 'This distinction — an absolute lack of insulin (Type 1) versus reduced tissue sensitivity to insulin (Type 2) — explains why the two conditions are managed differently: Type 1 always requires insulin replacement, while Type 2 can sometimes be managed initially through lifestyle changes that improve insulin sensitivity, before medication or insulin becomes necessary.',
