          prompt: 'Name the TWO naturalists who independently proposed the theory of evolution by natural selection, and name the book, published in 1859, in which one of them set out the theory.',
          answer: 'Charles Darwin and Alfred Russel Wallace; On the Origin of Species (by Means of Natural Selection).',
          explanation: 'Two people arriving at the same explanation from different evidence is itself a lesson in how science works, and it is the historical anchor for the whole evolution section.',
