          marks: 3,
          prompt: 'Name the technique that uses the decay of radioactive carbon-14 to estimate the age of a fossil, state the kind of material it can be used on, and state ONE limitation of the technique.',
          answer: 'Radiocarbon dating (a form of radiometric dating); it is used on material that was once living and still contains carbon; it is only reliable for material younger than roughly 50 000 to 60 000 years, so older fossils must be dated by other isotopes such as potassium-argon.',
          explanation: 'Dating is what turns a collection of fossils into a sequence, and knowing the limit of carbon-14 explains why the ages of hominin fossils are quoted from other methods.',
