          label: '4.1',
          topicId: 'life-sci-evolution',
          grade: 12,
          difficulty: 'Easy',
          cognitiveLevel: 1,
          marks: 2,
          prompt: 'Define evolution.',
          answer: 'Evolution is the gradual change in the genetic (allele) composition of a population over successive generations.',
          explanation: 'Evolution occurs at the level of the population, not the individual — an individual organism does not evolve during its own lifetime, but the allele frequencies within a population can change over many generations.',
