          cognitiveLevel: 1,
          marks: 3,
          prompt: 'Name the region of a plant shoot in which auxin is produced, and state the effect that auxin has on the cells of the elongation zone below it.',
          answer: 'The shoot tip / apex (apical meristem) (1). Auxin stimulates the cells in the elongation zone to absorb water and elongate (grow longer) (2).',
          explanation: 'Where auxin is made and what it does to cells is the recall foundation for every tropism explanation, including why a shaded side of a stem grows faster.',
