          cognitiveLevel: 3,
          marks: 4,
          prompt: 'Explain why people with untreated hyperthyroidism (an overactive thyroid gland) often experience unexplained weight loss despite eating normally.',
          answer:
            'An overactive thyroid produces excessive thyroxine, which increases the body’s basal metabolic rate (the rate at which cells use energy for basic functions). Since cells are burning through energy (and hence food/stored fat) faster than normal, a person can lose weight even while eating a normal amount, because their body is consuming energy at an abnormally high rate.',
