          explanation: 'Because this entire process (variation, selection, and a resulting change in allele frequency) can be directly observed happening in real time in a laboratory or clinical setting, antibiotic resistance is considered one of the clearest and most directly observable pieces of evidence for natural selection actually occurring, rather than evidence that must be inferred from historical or indirect data.',
