          difficulty: 'Easy',
          cognitiveLevel: 1,
          marks: 3,
          prompt: 'Name the type of rock in which fossils are most commonly found, and name TWO kinds of remains or traces of an organism that can be preserved as fossils.',
          answer: 'Sedimentary rock (1); any TWO of: bones or teeth (1); shells or other hard parts (1); footprints, burrows or other trace fossils (1); imprints of leaves, casts or moulds, or preserved wood (1).',
          explanation: 'Sediments settle in layers and slowly harden, burying remains gently enough for them to be preserved. Hard parts such as bones, teeth and shells survive best, but traces of activity such as footprints and burrows, and imprints of soft structures such as leaves, can also be preserved.',
