          marks: 3,
          prompt: 'State what is meant by the half-life of a radioactive isotope, state whether radiometric dating gives the absolute or the relative age of a fossil, and state what is meant by the relative age of a fossil.',
          answer: 'The half-life is the time taken for half of the atoms of the radioactive isotope in a sample to decay (1); radiometric dating gives the absolute age (1); the relative age is the age of a fossil expressed as older or younger than another fossil, rather than as a number of years (1).',
