          prompt: 'Name the type of speciation that occurs when a population is divided by a geographic barrier, name the type that occurs without any geographic separation, and name what must develop between the two groups before they can be regarded as separate species.',
          answer: 'Allopatric speciation (1); sympatric speciation (1); reproductive isolation (1).',
          explanation: 'Geographic separation gives allopatric speciation, while sympatric speciation happens within one area, for example through polyploidy. In both cases new species exist only once reproductive isolation prevents the groups from interbreeding to produce fertile offspring.',
