          marks: 3,
          prompt: 'State TWO ideas that formed part of Lamarck’s explanation of how species change over time, and state ONE reason why Lamarck’s explanation is rejected by scientists today.',
          answer: 'Any TWO of: organisms change during their lifetime through use and disuse of body parts (1); a structure that is used more becomes better developed and one that is not used degenerates (1); characteristics acquired during an organism’s lifetime are passed on to its offspring (1); reason for rejection: changes to body (somatic) cells are not passed on because only changes in the DNA of the gametes are inherited (1).',
          explanation: 'Lamarck proposed use and disuse together with the inheritance of acquired characteristics. Modern genetics shows that only alleles carried in the gametes are transmitted, so a characteristic developed during an individual’s own lifetime cannot be inherited.',
