          explanation: 'The Eustachian tube runs from the middle ear to the pharynx. When it opens, for example on swallowing or yawning, air moves in or out of the middle ear so that the pressure on the inner side of the eardrum matches the atmospheric pressure on the outer side, allowing the eardrum to vibrate freely.',
