          topicId: 'life-sci-endocrine-homeostasis',
          grade: 12,
          difficulty: 'Easy',
          cognitiveLevel: 1,
          marks: 2,
          prompt: 'Name the mineral that must be present in the diet for the thyroid gland to produce thyroxine, and name the swelling of the thyroid gland that develops when this mineral is lacking.',
          answer: 'Iodine (1); goitre (1).',
          explanation: 'Iodine is a component of the thyroxine molecule. Without enough dietary iodine the gland cannot make sufficient thyroxine, and the gland enlarges into a visible swelling in the neck known as a goitre.',
