          answer: 'Any TWO of: breeding at different times or seasons (1); differences in courtship or mating behaviour (1); differences in the structure of the reproductive organs, or gametes that are incompatible (1); offspring that are sterile or do not survive (1); reproductive isolation prevents the two populations from interbreeding to produce fertile offspring, so their gene pools cannot mix (1).',
