          prompt: 'State THREE reasons why the fossil record does not contain a complete record of all the organisms that have ever lived.',
          answer: 'Any THREE of: most dead organisms decompose or are eaten before they can be preserved (1); fossils form only under specific conditions, such as rapid burial in sediment (1); many fossils are destroyed by heat, pressure, erosion or earth movements (1); many fossils lie buried too deep to be found, or have not yet been discovered (1).',
          explanation: 'Fossilisation is a rare event that requires unusual conditions, and fossils that do form may later be destroyed or remain undiscovered. The record therefore preserves only a small, uneven sample of past life.',
