          prompt: 'State THREE conditions that favour the preservation of the remains of a dead organism as a fossil.',
          answer: 'Any THREE of: the organism is buried rapidly, for example in mud, sediment, ice, resin or volcanic ash (1); the remains are in an oxygen-poor (anaerobic) environment, so decomposers cannot act (1); the organism has hard parts such as bones, teeth or shells (1); the remains are not disturbed by scavengers, currents or earth movements afterwards (1).',
          explanation: 'Preservation depends on the remains being protected from decomposers and from physical damage. Rapid burial in an oxygen-poor setting, especially of hard body parts, allows minerals to replace the tissue before it decays.',
