          difficulty: 'Challenge',
          cognitiveLevel: 3,
          marks: 6,
          context: 'Emphysema destroys the walls between neighbouring alveoli, so that many small air sacs merge into fewer, much larger ones. A healthy pair of lungs presents a gas-exchange surface of about 70 m². In advanced emphysema this can fall to about 30 m². The total volume of air the lungs hold is not reduced, and may increase.',
