          explanation: 'The surface-to-volume relationship is the whole of the first half, and it is the same reason alveoli, villi and root hairs are all small and numerous. The second half corrects the intuitive but wrong idea that breathlessness means not enough air: the limiting factor is the AREA available for crossing, which is why a patient can have over-inflated lungs and still be short of oxygen.',
