          marks: 2,
          prompt: 'Define excretion.',
          answer: 'Excretion is the removal of metabolic waste products (substances produced by the body’s own chemical reactions) from the body.',
          explanation: 'Excretion is distinct from egestion (the removal of undigested food/faeces, which was never actually absorbed into the body’s cells), since excreted substances are true metabolic waste products.',
