          prompt: 'Define a vertebrate.',
          answer: 'A vertebrate is an animal that possesses a backbone — a vertebral column made up of a series of vertebrae — enclosing and protecting the spinal cord.',
          explanation: 'Vertebrates are traditionally divided into five main classes: fish, amphibians, reptiles, birds and mammals, each with distinguishing features adapting them to different environments and ways of life.',
