          answer: '(1) The thylakoid membranes are folded into stacks (grana), which increases the surface area available for chlorophyll and the light-dependent reactions. (2) The chloroplast is surrounded by a double membrane enclosing the stroma, a fluid matrix containing the enzymes needed for the light-independent reactions (Calvin cycle).',
