          cognitiveLevel: 2,
          marks: 4,
          prompt: 'Describe the structure of the glomerulus, and explain how this structure creates the high blood pressure needed for ultrafiltration.',
          answer: 'The glomerulus is a tightly coiled knot of capillaries supplied by an afferent arteriole (which is wider) and drained by an efferent arteriole (which is narrower). Because blood enters through the wider vessel faster than it can leave through the narrower vessel, blood pressure builds up within the glomerulus, and this raised pressure forces small molecules out of the blood and into Bowman’s capsule.',
