          explanation: 'Because ATP and NADPH cannot be stored for long within the chloroplast, the rate at which they are produced during the light-dependent reactions directly limits the rate at which the Calvin cycle can proceed, tightly linking the two stages of photosynthesis even though only the first stage directly requires light.',
