          prompt: 'Describe the structure of Bowman’s capsule, and explain how it collects the filtrate produced during ultrafiltration.',
          answer: 'Bowman’s capsule is a cup-shaped structure that surrounds the glomerulus (a knot of capillaries), with an inner and outer wall separated by a narrow space. As high blood pressure in the glomerulus forces small molecules out of the capillary walls, this filtrate collects within the space of Bowman’s capsule, before draining into the first section of the nephron tubule (the proximal convoluted tubule).',
