          answer: 'The male reproductive part of a flower is the stamen, made up of the anther and filament; an example structure is the anther, which produces pollen. The female reproductive part of a flower is the carpel (pistil), made up of the stigma, style and ovary; an example structure is the ovary, which contains the ovule(s).',
