          label: '5.1',
          topicId: 'life-sci-excretion',
          grade: 11,
          difficulty: 'Easy',
          cognitiveLevel: 1,
          marks: 2,
          prompt: 'Define homeostasis, and name ONE organ system involved in maintaining it.',
          answer: 'Homeostasis is the maintenance of a stable, constant internal environment within the body, despite changes in external conditions; the urinary system is one organ system involved in maintaining it, mainly through the regulation of blood water and salt content.',
