          marks: 6,
          context: 'Two plants grow in the same fynbos patch. One has a long, narrow, curved red tube of a flower, pollinated only by a sunbird whose bill matches that curve. The other has small, open, shallow flowers visited by many kinds of insect. A conservation report describes the specialised flower as "better adapted".',
