          prompt: 'State the general body shape used to identify an animal as belonging to the phylum Platyhelminthes (flatworms), and explain why this phylum is named accordingly.',
          answer: 'Flatworms have a flattened, ribbon-like body shape, with no distinct body cavity (coelom) between the outer body wall and the internal organs — this flattened shape is the origin of the phylum’s common name.',
