          explanation: 'Each of these three adaptations addresses a specific challenge that a purely aquatic organism would not typically face to the same degree: obtaining oxygen from air rather than water, preventing excessive water loss on land, and supporting and moving the full body weight against gravity without the buoyant support that water provides.',
