          explanation: 'This difference means yeast’s anaerobic respiration is sometimes called alcoholic fermentation, while the equivalent process in animal muscle cells is called lactic acid fermentation — both are forms of anaerobic respiration, but they follow different biochemical pathways with different specific waste products.',
