          answer: 'During the exponential (log) phase, the population grows very rapidly, with the population size increasing at an accelerating rate over time. Growth is so rapid during this phase because resources (such as food, water and space) remain abundant relative to the still relatively small population size, so there is little competition limiting reproduction, and the population’s growth rate is essentially unconstrained by resource availability at this stage.',
