          explanation: 'This economic and medical argument for biodiversity conservation is sometimes described in terms of the "genetic library" that biodiversity represents — once a species becomes extinct, any unique genetic and biochemical information it carried, including any potential medical applications, is permanently and irretrievably lost.',
