          answer: 'The axial skeleton is the part of the skeleton that forms the main vertical axis of the body, consisting of the skull, the vertebral column (backbone) and the rib cage (ribs and sternum).',
          explanation: 'The axial skeleton mainly protects the body’s central organs (brain, spinal cord, heart and lungs), while the appendicular skeleton (limbs and girdles) is mainly associated with movement.',
