          prompt: 'Define ‘double circulation’.',
          answer: 'Double circulation is a circulatory system in which blood passes through the heart twice for each complete circuit of the body: once through the pulmonary circulation (heart to lungs and back), and once through the systemic circulation (heart to the rest of the body and back).',
          explanation: 'Double circulation allows blood returning from the lungs, now rich in oxygen, to be pumped back through the heart at higher pressure before being sent out to the rest of the body, delivering oxygen more efficiently than a single-circuit system could.',
