          prompt: 'Describe the structure and function of collenchyma tissue.',
          answer: 'Collenchyma tissue is composed of living cells with unevenly thickened cell walls (thicker at the corners of each cell than elsewhere), which remain flexible rather than rigid. It provides flexible mechanical support to the growing, still-elongating parts of a plant, such as young stems and leaf petioles, allowing these parts to bend without breaking.',
