          answer: 'Ribosomes are very small, non-membrane-bound organelles composed of ribosomal RNA and protein, and occur either freely scattered in the cytoplasm or attached to the surface of the rough endoplasmic reticulum. They are the site of protein synthesis (translation), where the genetic code carried on messenger RNA is used to assemble amino acids in the correct sequence to build a polypeptide chain.',
