          answer:
            'A producer is an autotrophic organism that makes its own organic food through photosynthesis, forming the base of a food chain, for example, an acacia tree. A primary consumer is a herbivore that feeds directly on producers, for example, a kudu that browses on acacia leaves. A secondary consumer is a carnivore that feeds on primary consumers, for example, a leopard that preys on kudu.',
