          explanation: '(a) (7 000 ÷ 100 000) × 100 = 7%. (b) (630 ÷ 7 000) × 100 = 9%. Both values are broadly consistent with the commonly quoted “10% rule”, which states that, on average, only around 10% of the energy available at one trophic level is transferred to, and stored as biomass in, the next trophic level, with the remainder lost, mainly as heat produced during cellular respiration.',
