          explanation: 'The distinction to be clear about is that an enzyme LOWERS the activation energy while heat supplies more energy to clear it — two different routes to the same outcome. The comparison then answers itself: heat is indiscriminate and destroys proteins, so a cell needs a method that is selective and works at body temperature, which is exactly what an enzyme is.',
