          cognitiveLevel: 1,
          marks: 5,
          prompt: 'Describe THREE structural features of xylem vessel elements that adapt them for the efficient, one-way transport of water.',
          answer: 'Any three of: (1) They are dead at maturity, with no cell contents to obstruct the flow of water. (2) Their end walls break down, forming continuous, unobstructed tubes. (3) Their walls are strengthened with lignin, preventing the vessel from collapsing under the tension created during transpiration. (4) They are hollow, providing a wide, open channel for water to move through with minimal resistance.',
