          answer: 'Compact bone is dense and solid in structure, with very few visible spaces, and forms the outer layer of bone as well as the walls of the shaft (diaphysis) of a long bone, providing strength. Spongy (cancellous) bone has a porous, honeycomb-like structure with many small spaces (often containing red bone marrow), and is found mainly within the wider ends (epiphyses) of a long bone, making the bone lighter without significantly weakening it.',
