          answer: 'A ball-and-socket joint (e.g. the hip or shoulder joint) allows movement in multiple directions/planes, including rotation, giving it the widest range of motion of any joint type. A hinge joint (e.g. the elbow or knee joint) allows movement in only one plane, essentially just bending and straightening (flexion and extension), like the hinge of a door.',
