          explanation: 'These structural differences directly reflect their different functions: the capillary’s thin wall and narrow diameter suit it to the exchange of substances with tissues, while the artery’s thick, muscular wall suits it to withstanding and helping maintain high-pressure blood flow leaving the heart.',
