          difficulty: 'Moderate',
          cognitiveLevel: 2,
          marks: 5,
          prompt: 'Distinguish between pulmonary circulation and systemic circulation.',
          answer: 'Pulmonary circulation is the pathway of blood flow from the right side of the heart to the lungs (where blood picks up oxygen and releases carbon dioxide) and back to the left side of the heart. Systemic circulation is the pathway of blood flow from the left side of the heart to the rest of the body (where oxygen and nutrients are delivered to tissues) and back to the right side of the heart.',
          explanation: 'Together, these two circuits make up the “double circulation” of the human circulatory system, since blood passes through the heart twice during each complete circuit of the body.',
