          grade: 10,
          difficulty: 'Easy',
          cognitiveLevel: 1,
          marks: 2,
          prompt: 'Name the TWO broad categories of factors, together forming an ecosystem, and give ONE example of each.',
          answer: 'Biotic factors (the living organisms in the ecosystem, e.g. plants, animals, micro-organisms) and abiotic factors (the non-living components of the environment, e.g. temperature, water, sunlight, soil type).',
