          marks: 5,
          prompt: 'Compare the venation (arrangement of veins) typically found in a monocotyledonous leaf with that of a dicotyledonous leaf, and state ONE other feature, other than venation, that can be used to distinguish monocotyledonous from dicotyledonous plants.',
