          answer: 'A source is any part of the plant that produces or releases sucrose into the phloem, which in sugarcane is mainly the green leaves that are photosynthesising. A sink is any part that removes sucrose from the phloem in order to use it or store it, such as the growing root tips, the developing buds and the storage tissue of the stem. Sucrose is actively loaded into the sieve tubes at the source and unloaded at the sink, so it moves from source to sink, which may be upwards or downwards depending on where the sink lies.',
