          prompt: 'Name the organelle that contains digestive enzymes and breaks down worn-out organelles, and state what would happen to the cell if many of these organelles burst.',
          answer: 'The lysosome; if many lysosomes burst, their enzymes would be released into the cytoplasm and would digest the cell itself, destroying it.',
          explanation: 'Keeping powerful hydrolytic enzymes inside a membrane-bound sac protects the rest of the cell, which is why lysosomes are sometimes called the suicide bags of the cell.',
