          answer: 'Epithelial tissue, for example the epidermis covering the skin of the arm; connective tissue, for example the bone of the humerus or the tendon joining the biceps to the radius; muscle tissue, for example the skeletal muscle of the biceps; and nervous tissue, for example the motor neurons running in the nerves that supply the arm muscles.',
