          marks: 4,
          prompt: 'Name the connective tissue that binds the skin to the muscles beneath it and fills the spaces between organs, and describe TWO features of this tissue that suit it to that role.',
          answer: 'Areolar, or loose, connective tissue. It has a soft, semi-fluid matrix containing a loose, irregular network of white collagen fibres and yellow elastic fibres, so it is flexible and can be stretched and then return to shape, which allows the skin to be moved over the muscle without tearing. It is also richly supplied with blood vessels and contains defence cells such as macrophages, so it nourishes the epithelium above it and provides a site where invading micro-organisms can be attacked.',
